From 2e870e8f710ee3427a9bf09fffa979f15fa8f189 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban_complete: refuse a ship review card's
 completion that ship cannot read

`hermes-core-wt ship --review-task` lands a core PR only when the review card's
completion metadata carries exactly `verdict` ("approve"), a 40-hex `reviewed_sha`
equal to the PR head and `reviewed_pr`. Reviewers completed with `review_verdict`,
`review_outcome`, `reviewed_head` or a bare PR number instead. The card showed done
and approved, ship refused it later ("completion metadata verdict is None") and a
whole new review card was filed for the same head (PR1349, PR1222, PR1123).

New `hermes_cli/kanban_review_contract.py`, called from the kanban_complete tool
before the goal judge and any write:
- A card states the contract when its body names a core-fork pull request
  (daveey/hermes or example-org/hermes), `reviewed_pr` and the head key
  (`reviewed_sha`, or `reviewed_head` as some briefs misnamed it). Ship-filed and
  re-issued review cards do; so did the misnamed briefs that caused the re-issues.
- On such a card, a completion that is a review result (any of verdict,
  review_verdict, review_outcome, reviewed_sha, reviewed_head, reviewed_pr,
  approved, approval) must carry `verdict` in {approve, request_changes}, a
  lowercase 40-hex `reviewed_sha` and `reviewed_pr` as a pull URL or owner/repo#n.
  Otherwise it is refused with rejection class `review_contract`, naming each bad
  key and the alias that is not read; nothing changes, so the same run retries.
- Left alone: cards without the contract, a landing handoff (`published_pr`), and
  a completion with no review key (a card that only discusses the contract).

Layer: core, not the kanban-honest-done plugin. Pool workers run most review cards
and have no kanban-honest-done installed (hermes-worker-3's plugins.enabled lists
11 guards, not it), so a plugin gate would miss the hosts where the gap happens.
Ship is unchanged: no aliases, no inferred sha, exact-head check as before.

Proof:
- New tests/tools/test_kanban_review_contract.py (50 tests). The three tool-path
  tests (review_verdict only; no reviewed_sha; reviewed_head instead) fail with the
  tools/kanban_tools.py wiring reverted, and the file fails to import on main.
  A correct completion and a card without the contract complete.
- Mutants: 26 by exact anchor (contract detection clauses, repo restriction and
  case fold, published_pr/review-key exemptions, each key check, fullmatch vs
  match/search, isinstance guards, alias hints, tool raise, rejection class
  registration): all killed.
- 176 passed across 7 files (review contract, complete parents/receipt/rejection
  class, kanban_tools, watch park, foreign card writes).
- Read-only replay (mode=ro) of the latest completed run of every card completed
  in the last 14 days on the default-board replica (kanban/sync-shadow/default.db):
  5549 cards, 465 state the contract, 21 would have been refused (verdict 6,
  reviewed_pr 11, reviewed_sha 2, both 2). 3 of those 21 later needed a re-issued
  review of the same head (t_01a1ce2d6a3b3e75 PR1123, t_01a1ce6e03114795 PR1222,
  t_01a1cf47771fda0d PR1349); a fourth (t_01a1cf5a827ae485 PR1342,
  reviewed_pr=1342) completed during this work. 3 contract cards completed
  without review keys or with published_pr and stay unaffected. Of the 191 runs
  with `review_verdict` in 14 days, 4 were on contract cards and 13 on cards
  naming a core PR; the rest were other repositories' reviews.
